    ^{:line 210 :tag (array summaryLevels (slice pallocSum)) :doc "Radix tree of summaries.\n\nEach slice's cap represents the whole memory reservation.\nEach slice's len reflects the allocator's maximum known\nmapped heap address for that level.\n\nThe backing store of each summary level is reserved in init\nand may or may not be committed in grow (small address spaces\nmay commit all the memory in init).\n\nThe purpose of keeping len <= cap is to enforce bounds checks\non the top end of the slice so that instead of an unknown\nruntime segmentation fault, we get a much friendlier out-of-bounds\nerror.\n\nTo iterate over a summary level, use inUse to determine which ranges\nare currently available. Otherwise one might try to access\nmemory which is only Reserved which may result in a hard fault.\n\nWe may still get segmentation faults < len since some of that\nmemory may not be committed yet.\n"} summary





































